<p>Bit mask for up in the joystick readings <strong>joy1</strong> /
<strong>joy1pressed</strong> (and <strong>joy2</strong> / <strong>joy2pressed</strong> where a
second port exists), which are filled in by readjoy1() and readjoy2().</p>
<p>The bit value is not the same on every machine, so test with the constant
rather than the number.</p>

<p>Example</p>
<code>
readjoy1();

// true every frame up is held
if (joy1 &amp; JOY_UP) then y := y - 1;

// true only on the frame it was first pressed
if (joy1pressed &amp; JOY_UP) then y := y - 1;
</code>
<p>See also JOY_UP, JOY_DOWN, JOY_LEFT, JOY_RIGHT and JOY_FIRE.</p>
